{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE REWRITE WORKED, AND IT EXPOSED THE NEXT LAYER — run 30867072561\n\nChange 1330's approved fix (clear a non-sub-task's Epic Link instead of a sub-task's `fields.parent`) is live-proven on the REMOTE side. The cell no longer reports SETUP FAILED, and no longer dies on DC refusing the null. It now reaches its real assertion and fails there:\n\n    the DC Epic Link WAS CLEARED (confirmed absent from both the direct GET and the\n    search-backed parent map, which 9bb9 taught to read it)\n    but .parent_id on jira-rbjyvtm-2 is still 'jira-rbjyvtm-1'\n\n**That is progress of exactly the kind this ticket was rewritten to buy.** The precondition is now reachable, the remote mutation happens, both read paths agree it happened — and the defect that was hiding behind the unreachable precondition is now visible: **the clear does not propagate to the LOCAL `.parent_id`.**\n\n### What this most likely is, stated as a hypothesis rather than a conclusion\n\n88d9's evidence-gated clear (`inbound_fields.diff_inbound_parent(peer_parent=...)` -> `if not peer_parent: decline`) exists so a Jira-dropped parent is only cleared on PEER evidence. If no peer parent is recorded for this pair, the clear is declined BY DESIGN and the local value correctly survives. If so this cell is asserting something the product deliberately does not do, and the cell — not the product — is what needs to change.\n\nI have NOT confirmed that. It is the first thing to check, and it is cheap: the peer-parent state at the moment of the pass decides whether this is a product gap or a cell that outran its own design. **Do not fix either side before establishing which.** That mis-step — repairing the visible symptom without proving the mechanism — is what produced 1276, 1288 and 1302.\n\n### The falsifiers ran again and reproduced EXACTLY\n\nThe cell now carries raw platform probes inline, and they match the capability map on a different instance and a different day:\n\n    raw PUT (fields form)      -> HTTP 204, body None\n    raw PUT (update-verb form) -> HTTP 400 \"Field 'parent' cannot be set. It is not on the\n                                  appropriate screen, or unknown.\"\n    /editmeta for 'parent'     -> HTTP 200, operations []\n\nSo the operator's ruling stands unchanged and is now doubly evidenced: DC still refuses the sub-task case, and the two forms still fail differently. The honest verdict on sub-task clearing remains **UNKNOWN, not NOT-RESOLVABLE**."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785808300920225001,"uuid":"9665f46b-a229-4ad4-bb44-2310da1af89e"}